{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>לענת</b> Twice in the Masorah: לענות נפש (Numbers 30:14), לענות והוא ענין כלי שיר — to say that if she vowed not to hear musical instruments, her husband may annul it, for it is considered like vows of afflicting the soul, as stated in Mo'ed Katan (9a) that even old women derive pleasure from musical instruments — a sixty-year-old like a six-year-old — from a fine, clear-sounding table (such is the wording there)."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The Hebrew citation 'לענות נפש על מחלת לענות' appears to cite two Masorah occurrences: לענות נפש and לענות (on מחלת); the second occurrence is in II Kings 6:33. The Aramaic gloss 'והוא ענין כלי שיר' explains לענות as referring to musical instruments."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:28.001561077Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}